  "finalReply": "Implemented `/app/validate_template.py` to detect and mitigate SSTI vulnerabilities.\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Accepts template path as argument; prints error to stderr and exits non-zero on missing arg, missing file, directory path, or read errors.\n- Extracts `{{ ... }}` / `{% ... %}` expressions (ignores `{# comments #}`, ignores plain text), handles malformed/unclosed tags gracefully.\n- Flags expressions containing `__`, or word-boundary matches for `eval`, `exec`, `import`, `globals`, `locals`, `getattr/setattr/delattr/hasattr`, `attr`, `os/sys/subprocess/importlib/builtins/inspect/ctypes/pydoc/shutil/socket/pathlib/pickle`, `system/popen/Popen/spawn`, `mro/subclasses/bases`, `request/config/lipsum/cycler/joiner`, `compile/open/chr/ord`, etc.\n- Allows safe constructs: `{{ variable }}`, `{{ user.name }}`, `{% for %}...{% endfor %}`, `{% if %}...{% endif %}`, `{{ value | upper }}`, `range()`, math, etc.\n- On dangerous content, overwrites file in place with exactly `REJECTED: Template contains dangerous expressions`; otherwise leaves file unchanged.\n\n**Verified:**\n- Safe templates (variables, loops, conditionals, filters, `user.name`/`user.id`/`range`) left unchanged, exit 0.\n- Dangerous payloads (`__class__.__mro__`, `eval()`, `os.system()`, `subprocess.Popen()`, `globals()`/`request`/`config`, `|attr`) all replaced with REJECTED text, exit 0.\n- Missing file / missing arg exit non-zero with error message; plain-text dangerous words outside tags and malformed templates handled without crash.",
